{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795295350,"nonce":"kySL8MRdjvNNTvebv3TK/ln0Y2I=","title":"Layer composite blend modes divide straight colour by alpha again","message":"draw_overlay_nodes straightens a layer (AlphaPass::straighten) before blit_tight_texture_to_target, so the composite shader's input is straight colour. The normal path in layer_composite.rs treats it that way (src.xyz * src_alpha). The blend-mode path does not: it computes src_c = src.xyz / src.w as if the input were premultiplied. For a layer with mix-blend-mode other than normal, any pixel with alpha below 1 (anti-aliased edges, translucent fills) comes out too bright before the blend function runs.\n\nNot reproduced yet. Found while reading the overlay layer path for git-bug 7936e4b. Check whether any caller passes a premultiplied texture with a blend mode before changing the shader; if none does, the blend path should use src.xyz directly.","files":null}]}